---json
{
  "lang": "en",
  "slug": "services",
  "title": "Work With Me — ISO 19650 Delivery &amp; AI Automation | Andrea Aita",
  "description": "Four ways to work together: AI and automation sprints for AEC workflows, information management strategy, BEP and EIR production, and embedded programme delivery leadership.",
  "ogTitle": "Work With Me — ISO 19650 Delivery &amp; AI Automation | Andrea Aita",
  "ogDescription": "AI and automation sprints, information management strategy, BEP and EIR production, embedded programme delivery. Scoped on the deliverable.",
  "ogImageAlt": "Andrea Aita — ways to work together",
  "calendly": true,
  "hasMirror": true
}
---
{% from "macros/blocks.njk" import sectionHead %}
<main id="main-content">

  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="page-hero-inner">
      <div class="hero-label">Ways to work together</div>
      <h1>Ten years of delivery, <em>and the ability to ship the fix.</em></h1>
      <p class="page-hero-sub">Most information management problems are already understood by the people living with them. What is missing is someone who can specify the fix precisely and then actually build it. That is the whole offer.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a href="{{ site.calendly }}" onclick="Calendly.initPopupWidget({url:'{{ site.calendly }}'});return false;" class="btn btn-primary btn--lg">Book a 30-min call</a>
        <a href="contact.html" class="btn btn-outline btn--lg">Send a brief instead</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-contact-note">Prefer email? <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="fade-in" aria-label="Engagements">
    {{ sectionHead("Engagements", "Four ways in", "Every engagement is scoped on the deliverable rather than the hour, and starts with a conversation about what is actually going wrong.") }}

    <div class="offer-grid offers-preview">

      <article class="offer-card offer-card--featured">
        <div class="offer-card-badge">Start here</div>
        <h3 class="offer-card-title">AI &amp; automation <em>sprints</em></h3>
        <p class="offer-card-intro">Move AI from the strategy deck to a live AEC workflow. One narrow, painful, repetitive process — picked because it is costing you real hours — specified tightly and put into production.</p>
        <div class="offer-card-price-section">
          <div class="offer-card-price">1&ndash;4 weeks <span>typical sprint</span></div>
          <div class="offer-card-price-note">Scoped on enquiry, priced on the deliverable.</div>
        </div>
        <ul class="offer-card-list">
          <li>AI-native tooling for tender, information management and document control</li>
          <li>Automation across PDFs, project data and delivery reviews</li>
          <li>A stakeholder demo with before-and-after proof, not a slide</li>
          <li>Handover, rollout roadmap, and the source code</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="builds.html" class="offer-card-link">See {{ builds.total }} public builds <span>&rarr;</span></a>
      </article>

      <article class="offer-card">
        <h3 class="offer-card-title">Information management <em>&amp; strategy</em></h3>
        <p class="offer-card-intro">The CDE exists but nobody uses it properly. Requirements are copy-pasted from the last job. Naming is inconsistent and reporting is manual. This fixes the framework rather than the symptoms.</p>
        <div class="offer-card-price-section">
          <div class="offer-card-price">Ongoing <span>or fixed scope</span></div>
          <div class="offer-card-price-note">Scoped on enquiry.</div>
        </div>
        <ul class="offer-card-list">
          <li>CDE workflow and governance design</li>
          <li>Naming conventions and data standards people will actually follow</li>
          <li>Reporting structures and supply-chain information requirements</li>
          <li>Capability assessment and adoption support across live teams</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="contact.html" class="offer-card-link">Talk it through <span>&rarr;</span></a>
      </article>

      <article class="offer-card">
        <h3 class="offer-card-title">BEP &amp; EIR <em>production</em></h3>
        <p class="offer-card-intro">BEPs take weeks, start from a blank template, and miss half the EIR. EIRs come back vague enough that the supply chain cannot price them. The gap between the two compounds through every stage.</p>
        <div class="offer-card-price-section">
          <div class="offer-card-price">Per document <span>pre- or post-appointment</span></div>
          <div class="offer-card-price-note">Scoped on enquiry.</div>
        </div>
        <ul class="offer-card-list">
          <li>Compliant, EIR-aligned BEPs without starting from blank</li>
          <li>EIR drafting and review for client-side teams</li>
          <li>Drafted with Capsar.io, so requirements stay traceable</li>
          <li>A walkthrough and a revision window included</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="capsar.html" class="offer-card-link">How Capsar helps <span>&rarr;</span></a>
      </article>

      <article class="offer-card">
        <h3 class="offer-card-title">Programme <em>digital delivery</em></h3>
        <p class="offer-card-intro">For programmes that need the capability in the room rather than in a report — embedded delivery leadership, or a retained advisor the team can escalate to.</p>
        <div class="offer-card-price-section">
          <div class="offer-card-price">Embedded <span>or retained</span></div>
          <div class="offer-card-price-note">Scoped to programme needs.</div>
        </div>
        <ul class="offer-card-list">
          <li>Embedded information management leadership</li>
          <li>Retained advisory for in-house teams</li>
          <li>Supply-chain readiness and assurance</li>
          <li>Training — over 500 professionals to date</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="contact.html" class="offer-card-link">Discuss a programme <span>&rarr;</span></a>
      </article>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fade-in" aria-label="Selected engagements">
    {{ sectionHead("Proof", "Selected engagements", "Anonymised, because most of this work sits under NDA. The shape of the problem is the useful part.") }}

    <div class="value-props">
      <div class="value-card value-card--half">
        <h3>National infrastructure programme</h3>
        <p>Digital delivery framework built from scratch across a multi-party programme — CDE governance, information standards, and the assurance process that kept them honest once the framework left the room.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card value-card--half">
        <h3>Tier 1 contractor bid</h3>
        <p>BEP production against a live tender deadline, aligned to a demanding EIR. Delivered as a submission-ready package rather than a template the bid team still had to finish.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card value-card--half">
        <h3>EIR review &amp; supply-chain readiness</h3>
        <p>Client-side EIR rewritten so the supply chain could respond against it, followed by a readiness assessment of the responding parties — closing the gap before it reached appointment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card value-card--half">
        <h3>CDE governance &amp; reporting</h3>
        <p>A regional contractor with a CDE nobody trusted. Workflows, naming and automated reporting rebuilt around how the team actually worked, then adopted rather than mandated.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fade-in" aria-label="How an engagement runs">
    {{ sectionHead("Process", "Three steps from enquiry to delivery", "No lengthy forms, no discovery theatre, and no proposal that takes a fortnight to arrive.") }}

    <div class="value-props">
      <div class="value-card value-card--third value-card--feature">
        <h3>01 &nbsp;Brief</h3>
        <p>Tell me what you are working on — project type, stage, and what is actually hurting. Thirty minutes on a call is usually enough to know whether I am the right person.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card value-card--third">
        <h3>02 &nbsp;Scoped</h3>
        <p>I review your EIR, requirements or workflow, clarify the scope, and confirm the deliverable and the timeline in writing before anything starts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card value-card--third">
        <h3>03 &nbsp;Delivered</h3>
        <p>You get a working output — document, framework, or running software — with a walkthrough and a revision window. Where it is code, you get the repository.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fade-in" aria-label="Common questions">
    {{ sectionHead("Common questions", "Before you book") }}

    <div class="value-props">
      <div class="value-card value-card--half">
        <h3>Do you work outside the UK?</h3>
        <p>Yes. I am London-based and work across the UK and EU, remotely by default, on site where the work genuinely needs presence. I work in English and Italian.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card value-card--half">
        <h3>Why is there no price list?</h3>
        <p>Because the same job title covers a two-day review and a six-month programme. Rates depend on scope, urgency and depth of rollout — you get a number in writing after the first call, before any commitment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card value-card--half">
        <h3>Who owns what you build?</h3>
        <p>You do. Sprint work ships with the source code and a handover. Nothing is locked to a platform you have to keep paying me for.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card value-card--half">
        <h3>Is this just AI hype?</h3>
        <p>Judge it from the code. {{ builds.TotalWord }} public repositories are on <a href="builds.html">the Builds page</a> — specify tightly, let agents do the volume, gate everything behind tests. Read them and argue with them.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="capsar-banner fade-in">
    <div class="capsar-banner-inner">
      {{ sectionHead("Next step") }}
      <h2>Thirty minutes is usually enough to tell.</h2>
      <p>Bring the problem, not a brief. If I am not the right person for it, I will say so on the call and point you at someone who is.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions hero-actions--center">
        <a href="{{ site.calendly }}" onclick="Calendly.initPopupWidget({url:'{{ site.calendly }}'});return false;" class="btn btn-primary">Book a 30-min call</a>
        <a href="contact.html" class="btn btn-outline">Send a brief</a>
      </div>
      <div class="capsar-badge">{{ site.email }}</div>
    </div>
  </div>

</main>
